.TH SCREENSENSE 1 "November 2026" "screensense 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
screensense \- move focus to the monitor you are looking at
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B screensense
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B screensense
uses the webcam to see which monitor you are facing, and moves keyboard focus,
the mouse pointer, or both there. It does not switch while you are typing or
using the mouse. Video is processed on this computer only and is never stored
or sent anywhere.
.PP
It normally runs as a systemd user service. On GNOME, a Shell extension changes
focus on its behalf and shows a camera icon in the top bar, with switches for
what focus means, the look time and the wait after typing.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run the background service. This is the default.
.TP
.B calibrate
Look at each monitor in turn so ScreenSense learns your setup, then hold your
eyes still while turning your head, which shows whether eye tracking works with
your camera. Run it again after moving the camera or rearranging monitors.
.TP
.B debug
Show the live head direction, eye direction and decisions, without changing
focus. With
.BR \-\-act ,
change focus too.
.TP
.BR pause ", " resume ", " toggle
Pause or resume a running service. The camera is off while paused.
.TP
.B status
Print the running service's state. Exits with status 3 if it is not running.
.TP
.B cameras
List detected cameras. Infrared face-unlock cameras are skipped by automatic
selection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Use this configuration file instead of the default.
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " name"
Desktop backend:
.BR auto " (default), " gnome " or " null .
.TP
.B \-\-act
With
.BR debug ,
actually change focus.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of commands and options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/screensense/config.ini
Settings and calibration. Every key is optional. After editing, run
.BR "systemctl \-\-user reload screensense" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 for a usage error, 3 from
.B status
when the service is not running, and 130 when calibration is cancelled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR gnome\-extensions (1)
.PP
https://github.com/AravindEdakkot/screensence
